  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nAfter upgrading What's Up Docker (WUD) from 8.4.0 to 9.0.0, the WUD widget on my Homarr board stopped working, throwing:\n\nTRPCClientError: Response from integration did not indicate success\n\nExpected: the widget should keep displaying the list of containers with available updates, like it did before the WUD upgrade.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Run WUD 9.0.0 with` WUD_AUTH_ADMIN_USER`/`WUD_AUTH_ADMIN_PASSWORD `set (mandatory auth introduced in 9.0.0, no legacy `WUD_AUTH_BASIC_* `vars configured)\n2. Configure the Homarr WUD integration with Basic Auth, using these admin credentials, integration URL http://wud:3000 (internal Docker network)\n3. Save the integration \u2014 connection test passes (\"Tested connection successfully\" in Homarr logs)\n4. Add/view the WUD widget on a board \u2192 error\n\n### Impact\n\nNot blocking (Homarr itself works fine otherwise), but the WUD widget is completely unusable after this upgrade \u2014 no workaround found so far besides removing the widget.\n\n### Additional information\n\nThe connection test succeeds, but the widget's actual data fetch fails \u2014 these seem to use different code paths, and only the data-fetching one is broken. Possibly a response schema/format change in WUD 9.0.0 that the widget doesn't expect yet.\n\nWhat works (tested manually against the WUD API):\n- curl -u admin:<password> http://wud:3000/api/app \u2192 200, {\"name\":\"wud\",\"version\":\"9.0.0\"}\n- curl -u admin:<password> http://wud:3000/api/containers \u2192 200, full container list as JSON\n\nHomarr logs on integration save:\nTesting connection... integrationKind=\"wud\" integrationUrl=\"http://wud:3000\"\nTested connection successfully... integrationKind=\"wud\" integrationUrl=\"http://wud:3000\"\n\nHappy to provide more details (network requests, exact response bodies) if useful.\n\n### Version\n\n1.77.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
